# The eval suite's CLI shim is SOURCE, not a build output, and `bin/` above
# swallows it silently: the commit that first introduced one went through
# without it, so the committed recipe pointed every operator at a directory
# that is not there, and the run graded whichever tla-spec-dev they happened to
# have installed -- the exact defect the shim exists to prevent, restored by
# the ignore file.
!evals/bin/
!evals/bin/**

# What a run produces, as opposed to what makes one. `evals/run.sh` harvests
# each run's report back out of the throwaway view into here.
evals/results/

# The MATERIALISED toolchain: checkouts of the units pinned in
# `evals/lib/toolchain.lock.toml`, fetched at their pinned commits by
# `evals/lib/toolchain.py`. THE PIN IS SOURCE AND IS COMMITTED; the checkouts it
# produces are derived and are not. They are also large -- skill-manager alone is
# 11,481 entries and 18M of .git -- which is why `evals/run.sh` excludes this
# directory from the staged view, whose entry ceiling is 20,000.
#
# IT IS AT THE ROOT AND NOT UNDER `evals/` DELIBERATELY: eval case discovery is
# a recursive glob over the eval dir, and the materialised skill-manager carries
# 56 case.yaml files of its own that would otherwise be discovered, scored and
# billed as this suite's.
.toolchain/

